          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What standards support secure electronics disposal?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS uses documented handling practices that support NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 media sanitization guidance, HIPAA-oriented disposal workflows, and chain of custody reporting. Project documentation can support internal records, vendor review, and compliance-focused technology disposition planning."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is business pickup available in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is available for qualifying business volumes in Bakersfield and throughout Kern County. Scheduling depends on equipment quantity, location access, equipment type, and service needs, so organizations should provide an inventory summary when requesting a pickup assessment."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide disposal documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Documentation may include chain of custody records, equipment lists, and Certificates of Destruction when data-bearing media is included. The appropriate reporting package depends on your organization's equipment, tracking requirements, and planned disposition method."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens after equipment is collected?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment is staged, transported, evaluated, and routed through documented recycling workflows. Reusable assets may be assessed separately, while data-bearing devices receive the agreed media-handling service before material recovery and downstream processing."
