      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/bakersfield-ca#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and standards do you reference?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS uses documented procedures that reference NIST SP 800-88 media sanitization guidance and support applicable HIPAA safeguards and California e-waste requirements. Project records can be structured for internal reviews, customer documentation, and regulatory audit support. These references address media handling, protected information, and state recycling obligations without treating every project as identical."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS serves Bakersfield, Kern County, and surrounding Central Valley communities through scheduled commercial pickup. Service planning can cover offices, campuses, healthcare sites, agricultural operations, warehouses, and public-sector locations. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near me in Bakersfield can request a project review for their equipment volume and access conditions."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup timing depends on equipment volume, site access, transportation requirements, and scheduling availability. Many qualifying projects can be planned within the same week after the equipment profile and pickup details are reviewed. Earlier planning is useful for campus refreshes, facility transitions, and recurring business equipment programs."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to equipment after pickup?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment is received, sorted, and routed according to its condition, material composition, and data requirements. Digital media can be documented for sanitization or physical destruction, while reusable materials may move through appropriate recovery channels. The resulting records can support asset reviews, environmental reporting, and internal disposition files."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup really free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is available at no charge for qualifying volumes and service conditions. Contact STS with the approximate equipment list, location, access details, and preferred timing so the team can confirm the appropriate arrangement. Equipment type, volume, loading requirements, and transportation needs affect the final service plan."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you handle recurring equipment refreshes?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Recurring projects can be organized around scheduled refresh cycles, equipment consolidation, facility transitions, or multi-site requirements. STS can help establish repeatable pickup instructions and documentation expectations for each project. This approach is useful for schools, healthcare networks, agricultural operations, and public agencies with recurring technology turnover."
          }
        }
      ]
